# TODO - EDMA/interrupts

## Objective

Implement ring allocation, IOMMU/DMA contracts, RX/TX ownership, descriptors,
completion, interrupt handling, memory safety, sleep and fault recovery in
source. Consult public ath9k and IOKit documentation. **No physical packet
transfer required.**

## Acceptance

- [ ] Implement/review the stated source and integrate on main.
- [ ] Bound DMA ownership, interrupts, completion and power-off quiescence.
- [ ] Ground decisions in public code, published standards and SDK/KDK references.
- [ ] Record unresolved assumptions and fail-closed behavior.
- [ ] Complete with source/static evidence, NEVER requiring a physical Dell test.

## Required source deliverables

- [ ] Allocate/map actual descriptor, status-ring and packet buffers through
      the provider's IOMMU/DMA contracts. Bound alignment, lengths, 32-bit
      device addresses and segment coverage; specify coherency/directions.
- [ ] Program RX/TX queues and doorbells, decode real completions and deliver
      actual received buffers. Metadata-only reservations are incomplete.
- [ ] Implement interrupt source/work-loop setup, masking/acknowledgement,
      deferred work and teardown, with no blocking hard-interrupt operation.
- [ ] Define publish/retire ownership, barriers and nonreused generations for
      every ring/buffer. Handle stale completions, overflow/underrun, queue
      pressure and reset without double free, reuse or unbounded waits.
- [ ] Quiesce producers/interrupts/device DMA before releasing mappings on
      failure, stop and sleep. Quarantine uncertain ownership; implement the
      real cleanup/recovery path and fresh resume generations.

## Start here and next implementation step

Ar9003Descriptors.* and Ar9003TxControl.* encode/decode fields; Ar9003Dma.*
tracks portable slots/generations. NativeDmaBuffer stages device-specific
IOMapper/IODMACommand packet resources behind a disabled macro. None programs
live queue/status rings or installs an interrupt source in the service.

Implement coherent descriptor/status-ring allocations and native queue control,
then IRQ/deferred completion processing and backpressure. Connect each packet's
publish/retire token to real completion or proven quiescence. Keep blocking
allocation/sync/release outside the owner gate, with explicit worker lifetime
and epoch revalidation when returning under the gate. Map before publication;
stop producers and isolate hardware before retiring/freeing uncertain DMA.

The portable `Ar9003Dma` metadata stage now also has a bounded RX slot
lifecycle with unique nonwrapping tokens, completion/sync gates, explicit
quiesced retirement (a distinct non-packet `Quiesced` state) and independent
`FromDevice` descriptor-ring mapping
checks. Synthetic C++14/C++17 sanitizer regressions pass. These are
owner-supplied attestations, not verified actual quiescence or completed RX.
TX also supports quiesced-but-unsuccessful retirement for device-owned slots
only after the native owner has actually stopped DMA and drained callbacks;
the native controller still must allocate/program coherent rings, synchronize
real mappings, identify the completed descriptor, drain interrupts and safely
publish the packet. This incremental source stage does **not** complete this
P1 TODO or authorize an active DMA path.

Primary references: [IODMACommand](https://github.com/apple-oss-distributions/xnu/blob/main/iokit/Kernel/IODMACommand.cpp),
[ath9k EDMA MAC/status](https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/master/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/ar9003_mac.c),
[RX queues](https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/master/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/recv.c),
and [TX queues/completion](https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/master/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/xmit.c).
Exact Tahoe API evidence remains required; Linux DMA addresses are not macOS
IOMMU mappings.

Choose interrupt type/index from the provider's actual capabilities; do not
assume a shared-line filter, MSI or MSI-X. If a primary filter is used, restrict
it to the minimal interrupt-safe source check/mask and deferred-work signal.
No allocation, command-gate invocation, NVM/reset polling or generic IOKit
callbacks belong there. Define acknowledgement/rearm ordering and a bounded
deferred-work budget so a stuck interrupt cannot monopolize the work loop.
Disable/unregister and synchronize pending delivery before releasing the
filter's owner or MMIO storage; masking alone does not drain callbacks.

Apple's [filter-interrupt contract](https://github.com/apple-oss-distributions/xnu/blob/main/iokit/IOKit/IOFilterInterruptEventSource.h)
describes primary-context restrictions; its
[command-gate contract](https://github.com/apple-oss-distributions/xnu/blob/main/iokit/IOKit/IOCommandGate.h)
forbids gate invocation from interrupt context. These public contracts guide
the source design; exact 25G332 declarations/exports still need A1 evidence.

Useful fake tests: checksum-valid malformed descriptors, wrong queue/generation,
ring wrap/full pressure, incomplete completion, failed mapping/prepare/complete,
and IRQ/stop/sleep interleavings without freeing hardware-owned memory.

## Evidence

- Source commits, reference URLs/version/rights, static review and lint diagnostics.
- Theoretical completeness only; no kext build, device scan, packet logs or hardware claims.
- Add offline host tests only where material behavior/error paths warrant them;
